    "title": "The Town That Has Been on Fire Since 1962 🔥🇺🇸 Centralia",
    "description": "Under Centralia, Pennsylvania 🇺🇸, a coal mine fire started in 1962, and it's still burning today 🔥 Experts think it could burn for another 250 years. Around 1981 about 1,000 people lived there. In 1992 the state used eminent domain to condemn every building, and by the 2020 census only 5 residents were left 😱 The cracked Route 61 became the famous 'Graffiti Highway' before it was buried under dirt in 2020.",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "A fire that has been burning for 60+ years 🔥😱",
